rel, main, clips, secs, mb = sys.argv[1:6]
D = '/home/claude/devtools/'
h = open(D + 'HANDOFF.md', encoding='utf8').read()

# title
h = re.sub(r'^# Hanashimashō — handoff \(.*?\n', "# Hanashimashō — handoff (18 Nov 2026, night, version 0.29.0 LIVE, main = %s, 39,666 of 39,666 clips; N1 grammar and kanji are COMPLETE; Usap Tayo 3.19.0 live and untouched in this chat; next = **1.0.0** (N1 extras and unit reviews, her decision of 18 Nov 19:26), see section 7)\n" % main, h, count=1, flags=re.M)

b3 = """- **0.29.0 (N1, second half: N1 complete).** Content plus two small code changes. Lessons `lessons-53..60.js` (24, ids `n1-*`, one unit of 3 per file, no `after`; plan `write/briefs-0.29/N1-LESSON-PLAN-2.md`): units Purpose, dependence and defiance; Occasions, pretexts and turning points; Surprise, emphasis and giving up; Concession and half-commitment; Relations, lists and word-building; Limits, missed chances and restraint; Old forms that are still alive; Formal Japanese at work (n1-keigo-3, n1-ronbun, n1-aisatsu). About a third of the planned patterns were already taught at N2 and became three-line reminders with links (the reports list them); n1-te-made teaches 〜なりとも and 〜が 関の山 だ (added by its writer, accepted). Kanji `kanji-n1f..j.js` (576, lists `write/briefs-0.29/n1f..j.txt`; registered after kanji-n1e.js): 2,225 kanji in all, N1 1,176; many are name kanji with "(given name)" / "(surname)" words. **Stroke data for N1 is in TWO sets**: `strokes/n1.js` (the first 600 N1 kanji in file order) and `strokes/n1b.js` (the rest); `setOf` in js/strokes.js picks `n1b` for N1 kanji after the first 600 of `App.KANJI` (so NEVER reorder or insert in kanji-n1a..e), `build-strokes.py` has the set `n1b`, sw.js precaches both. The "600 most frequent" line is gone from js/kanji.js. Dictionary `dict-n1-4..7.js` (1,202 words; registered after dict-n1-3.js; append only from now on): 7,249 words, 1,814 at level N1. Readings `reading-6.js` (4 clinical: shourei-houkoku, setsumei-doui-bunsho, iryou-anzen-dayori, kaifuku-no-shuki) and `reading-7.js` (shasetsu-kodoku, shikiten-no-aisatsu, zuihitsu-hatsushimo, kenshuu-ichinen): 40 readings. Dialogues `dialogues-4.js` (6: gakkai-shitsugi, kujou-taiou, nenpai-no-kanja, tashokushu-kaigi, buchou-ni-houkoku, soubetsukai-no-aisatsu): 28. `listen-questions-7.js` (42; Object.assign; after -6). Examples `examples-21..23.js` (788 = every N1-level word of the FIRST-half dictionary files; the about 900 N1-level words of dict-n1-4..7 have NO example yet). `topic-sets-6.js` (8 sets, ids `n1-*`). Trainer: 44 verbs and 15 adjectives with `lv: 'N1'` appended to verbs.js (572 and 322). Drills (new files, N1 items only, ids permanent): `grammar-cloze-n1a.js` (c-n1-001…096, first-half lessons), `grammar-cloze-n1b.js` (c-n1-101…196, second-half lessons), `grammar-transform-3.js` (t-n1-001…040), `grammar-errors-n1.js` (e-n1-001…040), `word-pairs-3.js` (p-n1-001…060), `listen-reply-3.js` (r-201…215 `clin: false`, r-216…230 `clin: true`; no risk item). No engine change was needed: every drill page showed N1 as soon as it had items. Still without N1: Sound words, picture sets, lesson extras and unit reviews. New fictional people: 三浦さん (man in his eighties, retired school principal, widowed about half a year ago, poor sleep, has stopped calligraphy, thinks at times of going to his wife but intends nothing because of his grandchildren, next visit in two weeks), 福田さん (an inpatient's daughter; room changed without notice), 岡本先生 (conference chair), 太田さん (social worker), 坂本部長 (department head; near fall at a corridor step), 清水さん (colleague leaving), 青木さん (retired librarian, the recovery essay), 野口さん (neighbour in her eighties, the frost essay), 前田 (caller in r-203), and the unnamed man in his seventies of the sample case report (the conference dialogue is about him). Spacing conventions new in 0.29.0: する-nouns joined in all new files (but する-noun + いたします split, as lessons-45 does); `いかん`, `ものともせず`, `ともなると`, `思いきや`, `なりとも`, `しかるべき` one word; `ずじまい` joined to its stem; 〜く とも / 〜よう とも with とも as one token (n1-de-are keeps と も); `こそ すれ`; `この 上 ない`; `差し支え ない`; `との 報告`; `何 なり と`; `あらしめる` one word; set phrases in dictionary files have a space on both sides of a particle. Totals: 261 lessons in 66 units (Starter 6, N5 47, N4 64, N3 32, N2 64, N1 48), 2,225 kanji, 7,249 dictionary words, 4,074 example sentences.
"""
